This March marked just 8 years in Australia for me. 8 years! 8 years!! 8 years of my life, my youth I spent in another country.  Why Australia and not somewhere else? 
Oh well, Australia was kind enough to grant me a visa while others did not. Australia has always been kind and the country was kind to me when I wanted to see the world. I love Australia for its blue sky, its national parks and beaches and many many animal farms. The country is just not what i had imagined before arriving here and that's why I still love it. 
Everyday is still somewhat surprise.
Why not Vietnam? I would say why Vietnam? I have always wanted to move back to Vietnam; sometimes, it aches me not to be able to do it, but the last 8 years have taught me one thing, I can get whatever I want for my life, just not all at once. I still love the Vietnamese food, love the hustle and bustle even more.
I still love the chaos and the quiteness in the countryside sometimes. It's still and will always be my home country where i will come back to live one day, soon.
